{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "cues": [
    {
      "id": "self-tickle-cue-1",
      "transcript": "Why can their fingers make you laugh, but yours usually can't?",
      "file": "audio/self-tickle/narration/cue-1.wav",
      "start": 0,
      "duration": 3.825,
      "beatIndex": 0,
      "sourceScriptSegmentId": "self-tickle.asset.perception.script.1",
      "samples": 91800,
      "sampleRate": 24000
    },
    {
      "id": "self-tickle-cue-2",
      "transcript": "Both touch your skin. One important clue is prediction.",
      "file": "audio/self-tickle/narration/cue-2.wav",
      "start": 4,
      "duration": 3.625,
      "beatIndex": 1,
      "sourceScriptSegmentId": "self-tickle.asset.perception.script.2",
      "samples": 87000,
      "sampleRate": 24000
    },
    {
      "id": "self-tickle-cue-3",
      "transcript": "When you move your hand, your nervous system can anticipate the touch it will produce.",
      "file": "audio/self-tickle/narration/cue-3.wav",
      "start": 7.8,
      "duration": 4.975,
      "beatIndex": 2,
      "sourceScriptSegmentId": "self-tickle.asset.perception.script.3",
      "samples": 119400,
      "sampleRate": 24000
    },
    {
      "id": "self-tickle-cue-4",
      "transcript": "That touch can feel weaker. Scientists call this sensory attenuation.",
      "file": "audio/self-tickle/narration/cue-4.wav",
      "start": 13,
      "duration": 4.775,
      "beatIndex": 3,
      "sourceScriptSegmentId": "self-tickle.asset.perception.script.4",
      "samples": 114600,
      "sampleRate": 24000
    },
    {
      "id": "self-tickle-cue-5",
      "transcript": "In experiments, self-produced touch felt less ticklish than matching external touch.",
      "file": "audio/self-tickle/narration/cue-5.wav",
      "start": 18.033333333333335,
      "duration": 5.275,
      "beatIndex": 4,
      "sourceScriptSegmentId": "self-tickle.asset.perception.script.5",
      "samples": 126600,
      "sampleRate": 24000
    },
    {
      "id": "self-tickle-cue-6",
      "transcript": "Adding a delay to a robotic self-touch made it feel more ticklish.",
      "file": "audio/self-tickle/narration/cue-6.wav",
      "start": 23.533333333333335,
      "duration": 4.3,
      "beatIndex": 5,
      "sourceScriptSegmentId": "self-tickle.asset.perception.script.6",
      "samples": 103200,
      "sampleRate": 24000
    },
    {
      "id": "self-tickle-cue-7",
      "transcript": "But those experiments used light touch, not full-on tickle laughter.",
      "file": "audio/self-tickle/narration/cue-7.wav",
      "start": 28.033333333333335,
      "duration": 4.35,
      "beatIndex": 6,
      "sourceScriptSegmentId": "self-tickle.asset.perception.script.7",
      "samples": 104400,
      "sampleRate": 24000
    },
    {
      "id": "self-tickle-cue-8",
      "transcript": "You can give yourself a light, tickly sensation. Laughter-inducing tickling is harder to explain, and people differ.",
      "file": "audio/self-tickle/narration/cue-8.wav",
      "start": 32.56666666666667,
      "duration": 7.4,
      "beatIndex": 7,
      "sourceScriptSegmentId": "self-tickle.asset.perception.script.8",
      "samples": 177600,
      "sampleRate": 24000
    },
    {
      "id": "self-tickle-cue-9",
      "transcript": "Prediction is an important clue, not the whole answer.",
      "file": "audio/self-tickle/narration/cue-9.wav",
      "start": 40.166666666666664,
      "duration": 3.575,
      "beatIndex": 8,
      "sourceScriptSegmentId": "self-tickle.asset.perception.script.9",
      "samples": 85800,
      "sampleRate": 24000
    },
    {
      "id": "self-tickle-cue-10",
      "transcript": "Your nervous system doesn't just receive touch. It can anticipate your own.",
      "file": "audio/self-tickle/narration/cue-10.wav",
      "start": 44.03333333333333,
      "duration": 4.625,
      "beatIndex": 9,
      "sourceScriptSegmentId": "self-tickle.asset.perception.script.10",
      "samples": 111000,
      "sampleRate": 24000
    }
  ],
